WEBVTT

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.999
[Singing]

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.999
[Singing]

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.999
[Singing]

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.999
[Singing]

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.999
[Singing]

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.999
[Singing]

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.999
[Singing]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.999
[Singing]

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.999
[Singing]

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.999
Hello, everyone.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.999
Wow, it's been a while since we came

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.999
to you through a livestream.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.999
We missed you so much

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:20.999
that we're still trapped here at Munhak.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.999
We are.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.999
We're truly still at Munhak.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.999
I couldn't leave either.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.999
That's right.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.999
Ja, it took a while,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.999
so thank you very much for waiting.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.999
We spent all day filming,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.999
and it seems there was

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:35.999
a small camera problem.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.999
Thank you for understanding.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.999
We'll fill the next two hours with no regrets,

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.999
so trust us and follow along.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.999
Ja, shall we sit down?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.999
Did the MC change today?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.999
I sometimes use Hamin

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:52.999
as an emergency remedy.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:53.999
Right, right.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.999
He tends to sprint at the beginning.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:56.999
Ja, so...

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:57.999
speaking of that...

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:58.999
MC?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:02:59.999
Yes? How was it?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.999
First of all, I was immersed in it,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.999
so it was difficult. The afterglow...

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.999
Yes, the afterglow of Munhak.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.999
The afterglow.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.999
This is a little...

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.999
American-style.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.999
I was immersed in it. Yes.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.999
You said you even wrote a poem, right?

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.999
I wrote a poem.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:18.999
He wrote one.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:19.999
I did.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.999
I'll recite it for you.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.999
Why did you suddenly write a poem?

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.999
The thought suddenly came to me.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:26.999
The moment you woke up?

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.999
In the morning.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.999
How artistic.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:31.999
But it doesn't have a title.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.999
I'd like PLLI to name it. The title is open.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:35.999
The title is innocent for now.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.999
Innocent? Yes.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.999
My poem.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.999
The wind is light, and the sunlight lingers.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.999
In a cloudless sky, suddenly you remain.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.999
You remain.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.999
At the quiet sound in the distance,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.999
I gently close my eyes.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.999
O sparrow,

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.999
chirp away,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.999
as much as I have missed you.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.999
Wow.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.999
You wrote such a moving poem.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.999
It has so much atmosphere.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.999
Please interpret it for us.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.999
There isn't a formal interpretation.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.999
I said that seeing the weather

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.999
often makes me think of PLLI,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.999
and I thought PLLI must feel the same.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.999
After a concert, the afterglow lingers

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.999
and the memories keep returning.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.999
They stay with you for days,

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.999
especially after a concert.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.999
I looked at the sky,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:37.999
and there wasn't a single cloud.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.999
It was completely blue,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.999
and PLLI came to mind.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.999
The sparrows sounded so lovely.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.999
It's getting autumnal these days.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.999
They were chirping away,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.999
and I wondered whether they too

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:54.999
might be calling for someone

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.999
and missing them.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.999
That's what inspired it. So the sparrow is PLLI?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.999
It could be PLLI, or it could be me.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.999
Then let's title it 'Munhak Boy.'

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:04.999
That's not bad.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.999
Isn't Eunho the 'Munhak Boy' here?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.999
Ah, that title already exists.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:11.999
It's his YouTube username too.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:12.999
I see.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:13.999
Yes.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.999
But when you actually look at it,

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.999
it's just about staring at the sky,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.999
closing your eyes,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.999
and telling a bird to chirp.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.999
Turning something so ordinary

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:26.999
is an amazing skill.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.999
It is.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:29.999
That's the charm of poetry.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.999
Wow, I discovered a new side of you today.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:31.999
You really did.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.999
Doesn't it sound like modern poetry?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:34.999
Modern poetry? What do you mean?

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:35.999
I don't know about that.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.999
I simply looked at the sky

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.999
and heard birds.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:40.999
That's all.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.999
Turning that into this...

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.999
It feels so full of nature.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.999
It doesn't sound like Seoul to me.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.999
Right. It feels like

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.999
somewhere surrounded by nature.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:52.999
What was the setting?

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.999
I was simply looking

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.999
out the window,

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:58.999
thinking of ASTERUM.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:05:59.999
This was at my home.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.999
Were you lying by the window

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.999
or sitting? I was lying on the sofa.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.999
So you were lying on the sofa,

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.999
heard birds outside,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.999
and turned it into this poem.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.999
You clearly have talent.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.999
The wind is obviously light.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.999
It isn't heavy. That's true.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.999
And sunlight naturally lingers

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.999
for a long time.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.999
Every line is obvious.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.999
You thought of someone in a cloudless sky.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.999
Exactly.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.999
You made obvious words sound impressive.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.999
Then you closed your eyes at a quiet sound--

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.999
meaning you were sleepy.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.999
You took a nap.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.999
You heard the birds chirping

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.999
and simply told them to keep chirping.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.999
That's basically right. 'As much as I missed you.'

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:48.999
Anyway, it was lovely.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:49.999
Yes.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.999
Ja, but our MC Bonggu

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.999
has become much more expressive

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.999
through hosting.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:58.999
Honestly,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:06:59.999
I didn't know

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.999
he was this good with words.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:02.999
You think I speak well?

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.999
He writes very well too.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.999
You improve with practice.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:07.999
He's improved.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:08.999
He has.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:09.999
Of course I should improve.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.999
PLLI is suggesting a title:

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.999
'Obvious Words.'

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.999
That's good.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:16.999
It is.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.999
'Obvious Words.'

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.999
The sentiment has suddenly faded. What do we do?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.999
Once you hear the title

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:25.999
It sounds so natural, right?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:27.999
Right, right.

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.999
Not exactly an 'N-sense kid,'

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.999
but it's funny.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.999
'Obvious Words' has

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.999
a spoonful of T in the F sentiment.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:36.999
That's perfect.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.999
'Obvious Words.'

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:39.999
The title is T, but the content is F.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.999
That's true.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:42.999
But that's also the charm of poetry.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.999
Right, right.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:45.999
Exactly. Great.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:46.999
It has charm.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.999
I really like 'Obvious Words.'

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:49.999
Ja, so Bamby spent his time

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.999
writing 'Obvious Words.'

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.999
What did the other members do?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.999
On our days off...

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.999
what did I do? First,

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.999
I focused on recovering physically.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.999
I'm still not at one hundred percent,

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.999
but I'm almost fully recovered.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.999
We prepared so hard

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.999
that there was some damage,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.999
so I stayed busy recovering.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:14.999
I think everyone was like that.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.999
It was so intense that I was a little worried.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.999
You need some time to recover. I actually

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.999
really like things like this.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.999
But you were in great condition today.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:23.999
You were really good today. >> Yes.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.999
I'm still recovering,

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.999
though.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.999
Should we call it a temporary measure?

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:29.999
Like...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.999
sometimes things suddenly flare up,

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.999
and today my stomach suddenly...

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:35.999
the pit of my stomach started hurting.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:36.999
Why is everyone...

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.999
Your solar plexus hurt again? Yes, again.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.999
It happened to me too. I had a lot of acid

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.999
coming up, all the way to my throat.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:44.999
It came right up.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.999
But you don't need to worry.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.999
We take good care of one another

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.999
and make sure everyone eats well.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:53.999
That's all we wanted to say.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.999
And these days, I've also been

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.999
eating a lot.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:58.999
Oh.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.999
I don't even think about dieting.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:01.999
But you still don't gain weight.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.999
I do. I do! What? I ate chicken,

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.999
and earlier I ate jjajangmyeon. At home,

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.999
I eat whatever I want, including snacks.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:08.999
I've seriously been eating a lot.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.999
You normally barely eat those.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.999
Snacks? >> What kind do you eat?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:13.999
Twix.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.999
Twix? Wow, it was so good.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.999
What's Twix? Wow, chocolate?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.999
No, listen. >> I was just sitting at home,

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.999
and it was even late at night.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.999
But I was craving something sweet so badly.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.999
There was fruit, even apples,

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.999
but I didn't want that.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.999
I wanted chocolate sugar, or just

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:34.999
pure sugar.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.999
I was craving snack-food sugar so badly.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:38.999
So I really put it all

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:39.999
in my mouth.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.999
It was delicious. Oh, you normally

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:42.999
eat healthy food, don't you?

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.999
Maybe my body needs it right now.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.999
But Twix is delicious.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.999
The one in the blue wrapper?

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:53.999
No, the yellow one with red on it.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.999
I don't know. >> It's chocolate with caramel

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:56.999
inside.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.999
Oh, that one! That one.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.999
I think that's the extra-size one.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:03.999
I ate that. I ate the whole thing.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:04.999
It's rather big. Wow.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:05.999
But why do you suddenly have one

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:06.999
right now?

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.999
I keep things like that around.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.999
Even our producers...

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:12.999
Stay away.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.999
Is it illegal to have one or something?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.999
No, I was just wondering how—

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:17.999
why do you have it?

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:18.999
I was curious where...

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.999
Why did you happen to have one?

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:22.999
This is fun. >> So why was it

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:23.999
at your house?

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:24.999
I buy and keep things like that.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:25.999
You buy them but don't eat them?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.999
I bought Twix this time too,

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:28.999
at Costco.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:29.999
You don't eat things like that either.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.999
I don't, but

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.999
when I buy them, I put them

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.999
in the cabinet under the sink,

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.999
you know? So most of the time,

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.999
they expire.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:42.999
Right, right.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:43.999
I don't even remember when I bought them,

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:44.999
but they were nearly expired.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.999
But you don't check expiration dates.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.999
I do check those.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.999
I check them. >> That's a relief.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.999
I still eat it after the date passes.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.999
Then why even check?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.999
It's okay to eat. >> You know what's too much?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:57.999
A sell-by date and a use-by date

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:58.999
are different.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:10:59.999
Yes. But have you ever

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.999
experienced this?

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.999
Some were probably past even the use-by date.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.999
Well, earlier... yes.

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:06.999
Honestly, I still eat ramyeon.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:07.999
Right, right.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:08.999
You cook and eat ramyeon.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:09.999
Noodles are kind of...

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.999
No, hyung. Wait. That's not it.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.999
A few days ago, I...

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:14.999
Buldak-bokkeum-myeon...

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.999
I wanted ramyeon for the first time in ages,

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.999
so I searched around and found it.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.999
I cooked the noodles

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.999
and tried to add the sauce, but it

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:24.999
wouldn't come out.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:25.999
It had hardened.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:28.999
You can't help that with

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:29.999
liquid sauces.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.999
Yes, and it also depends on where

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:32.999
you store it.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:33.999
Really?

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:34.999
Right, right.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.999
So I threw it away.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.999
You had to. Not long ago,

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.999
I got sick after eating bread.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:41.999
You ate mold, remember?

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:42.999
Bread.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.999
Did I tell them that or not?

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:46.999
PLLI? >> Oh, they don't know.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.999
It's fine to tell them. You ate it

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:49.999
without knowing.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.999
I guess I didn't. I had an upset stomach.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.999
I got sick once recently.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:55.999
It was...

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.999
I think it was before the concert.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.999
