00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:50.999
There was none at all. None.

00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:56.999
Really? Wow, that's very honest.

00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:57.999
Hey.

00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:00.999
Oh.

00:34:01.000 --> 00:34:01.999
Oh. Okay, okay.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.999
Okay, great. Excellent reaction.

00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:05.999
Great, great.

00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:06.999
Because we rehearsed it so many times.

00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:08.999
We really did.

00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:09.999
Even during all those rehearsals...

00:34:10.000 --> 00:34:11.999
The first two or three times,

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:13.999
I stumbled a little.

00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:14.999
They asked me to match the beat exactly.

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.999
It was hard. But: one, two, three,

00:34:18.000 --> 00:34:20.999
four; one, two, three, four; one, two, three, four.

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:24.999
That was it. Matching it to the count...

00:34:25.000 --> 00:34:27.999
Right. >> We can hear that in our in-ears.

00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:28.999
The counting is audible.

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:29.999
We hear it.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.999
After doing it two or three times,

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:32.999
I'd mastered it.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:33.999
Yes.

00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:36.999
But they kept making me do it.

00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:38.999
They must have been nervous.

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:40.999
Right? I think we did it more than ten times.

00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:42.999
We rehearsed it more than

00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:43.999
ten times. >> You were fine with it?

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:46.999
I was fine, but they kept

00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:47.999
making me do it again and again.

00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:50.999
I thought they would.

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:51.999
You shot a lot of arrows, right? >> Yes.

00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:53.999
I shot a lot. While doing that,

00:34:54.000 --> 00:34:55.999
I learned a lot about how to make

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:57.999
