00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.999
Right. It was truly a voice finding light

00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:38.999
in the darkness.

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:40.999
Weren't you something of an intro fairy

00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:43.999
for this concert?

00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:44.999
I did many of the intros

00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.999
this time—'Wait for Me' too,

00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:48.999
and this one.

00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:50.999
Because your hair is long,

00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:52.999
I think it suited you

00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:53.999
even better.

00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:55.999
Right. So many things suited you perfectly.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:57.999
I think that's partly how it happened,

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:00.999
because my hair is long.

00:36:01.000 --> 00:36:02.999
No, it's because you're handsome, hyung.

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:03.999
Right. >> I don't think that's it.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:06.999
And with 'Wait for Me,'

00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:08.999
my part came first,

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:09.999
so it just happened to fit

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:12.999
perfectly.

00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:14.999
And the Eastern-style concept...

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:15.999
Ah, the Eastern-style concept.

00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:17.999
We'll discuss that later, right?

00:36:18.000 --> 00:36:20.999
Right. Please wait a moment.

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:22.999
I'm going to discuss everything one by one.

00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:25.999
We'll talk about that style later.

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:26.999
Ja, let's move on

00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:28.999
to the next topic.

00:36:29.000 --> 00:36:30.999
Next came 'Blossom Parade,'

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:33.999
and the major issue there was

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:35.999
Eunho's in-ear monitor.

00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:38.999
Eunho, at first...

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:40.999
Everything was fine through rehearsal, right?

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:43.999
Completely. Everything had been

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:46.999
perfect.

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:48.999
I really wanted to say this on the livestream:

00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:50.999
it wasn't the fault of any staff member,

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:52.999
member, or artist.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:56.999
We rehearsed an enormous number of times

00:36:57.000 --> 00:36:58.999
and had the whole setup perfect.

00:36:59.000 --> 00:36:59.999
Then the VCR played,

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:01.999
and ten seconds before hyung had to shoot

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:03.999
the arrow—right before

00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:06.999
the start—I suddenly couldn't hear anything.

00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:08.999
Nothing at all.

00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:11.999
I wondered what to do, but

00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:13.999
the show had already started.

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:16.999
So I somehow kept going.

00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:19.999
I had already sung the opening verse,

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:22.999
and then the choreography began,

00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:23.999
but I still couldn't hear properly.

00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:24.999
Mm.

00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:26.999
I couldn't hear through the in-ears.

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:28.999
It passed in such a blur that I don't know what I did.

00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:32.999
I kept going into 'Blossom Parade.'

00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:34.999
They urgently replaced my in-ears for that song,

00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:38.999
but suddenly all I heard was

00:37:39.000 --> 00:37:40.999
the click track.

00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:44.999
And the members were suddenly going like this.

00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:47.999
They were all moving to 'doom-doom,'

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:50.999
and Noah hyung was behind me,

00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:53.999
going, 'Oh—ha—doom-doom-doom.'

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:57.999
I joined in, but it was terrifying.

00:37:58.000 --> 00:38:00.999
If I'd said, 'Should we

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:02.999
start over?' it would have broken the flow.

00:38:03.000 --> 00:38:05.999
Everyone was already happily

00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:07.999
watching the show,

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:08.999
and the other members...

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:09.999
You must have been the most disappointed.

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:10.999
Right, right.

00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:12.999
I was disappointed.

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:14.999
You don't need to be,

00:38:15.000 --> 00:38:16.999
because you did so well.

00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:18.999
Honestly, I think only Eunho could

00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:19.999
have done it. He naturally has

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:21.999
a good ear.

00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:22.999
His ear is naturally good.

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:25.999
He barely even needs to hear it.

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:26.999
You pulled it off.

00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:28.999
I thought that was so cool.

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:31.999
So many thoughts went through my mind.

00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:32.999
I agonized over it.

00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:35.999
Should we start this over?

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:38.999
That little extra seasoning is good.

00:38:39.000 --> 00:38:40.999
He's been playing so much Rummikub lately...

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.999
Right now...

00:38:43.000 --> 00:38:44.999
You may ignore what I just said.

00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:45.999
There's nothing there.

00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:46.999
This is driving me crazy.

00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:47.999
That was a Noah-style joke.

00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:49.999
When did you...

00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:50.999
A Noah-style joke?

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:52.999
You said it was a Noah-style joke?

00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:54.999
Noah-style humor.

00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:56.999
Was that a joke?

00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:58.999
He loves it so much. Yes.

00:38:59.000 --> 00:38:59.999
He really loves it.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:00.999
Okay, okay.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:02.999
Ja, so anyway...

00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:04.999
I could hear the click track

00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:06.999
and the sound of my own

00:39:07.000 --> 00:39:09.999
singing. Only those two things.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:11.999
I couldn't hear any music.

00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:13.999
No beat at all.

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:14.999
I had one in-ear out, so I could faintly

00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:17.999
hear the members' voices.

00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:19.999
I used them to find the key.

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:21.999
Honestly, if it had been me,

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:23.999
I would have seriously wondered

00:39:24.000 --> 00:39:24.999
whether we should start over.

00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:26.999
Right. I...

00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:28.999
Afterward, I think I would have asked

00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:30.999
to do it one more time.

00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:32.999
I simply couldn't hear the in-ear.

00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:36.999
I practically listened to 'Blossom Parade' again.

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:38.999
Exactly. It was only possible because

00:39:39.000 --> 00:39:39.999
it was Eunho hyung.

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:42.999
No, no. In any case,

00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:44.999
I'm very relieved that we

00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:46.999
managed to finish it.

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:48.999
And fortunately, the next song

00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:51.999
was 'Hide and Seek.' We hid for a while,

00:39:52.000 --> 00:39:54.999
and since the title was 'Hide and Seek,'

00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:56.999
we hid well and then made our entrance.

00:39:57.000 --> 00:39:59.999
The narrative worked out

00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:00.999
perfectly.

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:02.999
Do you know what's even more amazing?

00:40:03.000 --> 00:40:04.999
We performed 'Hide and Seek' next,

00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:06.999
and the wait ran long, so we were hidden.

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:07.999
While we were hiding, Eunho kept

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:09.999
adjusting his in-ears.

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:11.999
Then they clicked into place, and he went

00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:13.999
straight out to sing.

00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:15.999
Let's give him a round of applause. Amazing.

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:18.999
Thank you. But this is also

00:40:19.000 --> 00:40:20.999
the beauty of live performance.

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.999
I mentioned it on Bubble too.

00:40:23.000 --> 00:40:24.999
Because we work so hard

00:40:25.000 --> 00:40:27.999
to prepare for live performance,

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:29.999
not just I, but all the members

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.999
can respond to unexpected situations

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:34.999
like this. That's part of

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:35.999
the appeal of performing live.

00:40:36.000 --> 00:40:36.999
Right. Yes.

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:40.999
Anyway, that's what happened. What a relief.

00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:41.999
Nice.

00:40:42.000 --> 00:40:44.999
We're doing well.

00:40:45.000 --> 00:40:46.999
Ja. >> Ja, great. Let's move on.

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:48.999
We're making progress. Ja...

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:50.999
Let's talk about 'Hmpf!'

