01:17:36.000 --> 01:17:37.999
He even flew a drone

01:17:38.000 --> 01:17:39.999
to shoot it. Seriously.

01:17:40.000 --> 01:17:40.999
Because otherwise, he couldn't

01:17:41.000 --> 01:17:42.999
explain the view.

01:17:43.000 --> 01:17:44.999
Yejun couldn't believe it either.

01:17:45.000 --> 01:17:47.999
Where did you fly the drone?

01:17:48.000 --> 01:17:49.999
In the company's practice room.

01:17:50.000 --> 01:17:51.999
A small drone.

01:17:52.000 --> 01:17:53.999
The ceiling wasn't very high,

01:17:54.000 --> 01:17:57.999
so the blades scratched it a little.

01:17:58.000 --> 01:17:59.999
That was supposed to be secret.

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:01.999
It's a good anecdote. It's okay.

01:18:02.000 --> 01:18:04.999
When I saw it, I thought again,

01:18:05.000 --> 01:18:05.999
'That's impressive.'

01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:08.999
But seriously, what was I supposed to do?

01:18:09.000 --> 01:18:10.999
When we saw the actual stage,

01:18:11.000 --> 01:18:12.999
we watched it on the monitor too,

01:18:13.000 --> 01:18:14.999
because we have to monitor the show.

01:18:15.000 --> 01:18:16.999
The angles...

01:18:17.000 --> 01:18:17.999
Yes.

01:18:18.000 --> 01:18:21.999
The way every camera angle was found

01:18:22.000 --> 01:18:22.999
was completely insane.

01:18:23.000 --> 01:18:25.999
It went snap, snap, snap. Wow.

01:18:26.000 --> 01:18:26.999
This is incredible.

01:18:27.000 --> 01:18:29.999
In more technical terms,

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:31.999
it's sometimes called a previs cam.

01:18:32.000 --> 01:18:33.999
Maybe I shouldn't say that.

01:18:34.000 --> 01:18:35.999
Ah, yes. I mean, we pre-plan

01:18:36.000 --> 01:18:39.999
the intended direction and camera shots

01:18:40.000 --> 01:18:42.999
and rehearse with them.

01:18:43.000 --> 01:18:44.999
We do things like that.

01:18:45.000 --> 01:18:45.999
I had aligned many of them.

01:18:46.000 --> 01:18:48.999
We did a lot. >> Yes, we matched many shots.

01:18:49.000 --> 01:18:51.999
As far as I know, Hamin was

01:18:52.000 --> 01:18:52.999
the first to finish preparing.

01:18:53.000 --> 01:18:54.999
Right, right.

01:18:55.000 --> 01:18:56.999
But Hamin...

01:18:57.000 --> 01:18:59.999
The other members aligned their cameras well too,

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:00.999
but...

01:19:01.000 --> 01:19:02.999
we set up every shot one by one,

01:19:03.000 --> 01:19:05.999
and Hamin's were planned

01:19:06.000 --> 01:19:07.999
in extraordinary detail.

01:19:08.000 --> 01:19:10.999
Shot by shot—the key movements,

01:19:11.000 --> 01:19:12.999
like a hand gesture,

01:19:13.000 --> 01:19:14.999
were captured in precise detail,

01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:15.999
one by one.

01:19:16.000 --> 01:19:16.999
Right, exactly.

01:19:17.000 --> 01:19:18.999
Honestly, it felt almost pre-produced.

01:19:19.000 --> 01:19:19.999
That was the feeling.

01:19:20.000 --> 01:19:21.999
Right, exactly that.

01:19:22.000 --> 01:19:23.999
Seriously, how did every shot match?

01:19:24.000 --> 01:19:25.999
It looked like a stage assembled

01:19:26.000 --> 01:19:27.999
from only the best takes

01:19:28.000 --> 01:19:30.999
after filming it several times.

01:19:31.000 --> 01:19:31.999
It was so...

01:19:32.000 --> 01:19:32.999
I'd been thinking about it

01:19:33.000 --> 01:19:33.999
for a long time.

01:19:34.000 --> 01:19:34.999
You had. And I thought about

01:19:35.000 --> 01:19:37.999
how much you must have listened to the song alone

01:19:38.000 --> 01:19:38.999
and imagined

01:19:39.000 --> 01:19:40.999
the stage.

01:19:41.000 --> 01:19:42.999
I could feel that you'd designed it

01:19:43.000 --> 01:19:44.999
with excitement.

01:19:45.000 --> 01:19:45.999
It was cool, but almost too inhuman.

01:19:46.000 --> 01:19:47.999
That's because it was 'Spider' too.

01:19:48.000 --> 01:19:49.999
A spider, right.

01:19:50.000 --> 01:19:51.999
A spider.

01:19:52.000 --> 01:19:52.999
Yes, a spider.

01:19:53.000 --> 01:19:54.999
Because I performed alone,

01:19:55.000 --> 01:19:56.999
I think I paid even more attention

01:19:57.000 --> 01:19:58.999
to the cameras.

01:19:59.000 --> 01:20:00.999
I was the only person being shown.

01:20:01.000 --> 01:20:03.999
I focused on interpreting the song

01:20:04.000 --> 01:20:04.999
and its lyrics, and changed

01:20:05.000 --> 01:20:06.999
a lot of choreography. >> It was insane.

01:20:07.000 --> 01:20:09.999
For the acrobatic sections,

01:20:10.000 --> 01:20:11.999
we discussed how I could express

01:20:12.000 --> 01:20:13.999
a spider more clearly.

01:20:14.000 --> 01:20:14.999
I consulted with many people,

01:20:15.000 --> 01:20:16.999
received lots of ideas,

01:20:17.000 --> 01:20:18.999
and worked them in.

01:20:19.000 --> 01:20:20.999
It was flawless. Didn't it become complete?

01:20:21.000 --> 01:20:22.999
I have a question. >> It truly had no flaws.

01:20:23.000 --> 01:20:23.999
Whose idea was performing barefoot?

01:20:24.000 --> 01:20:25.999
The bare feet? Seriously,

01:20:26.000 --> 01:20:28.999
that was entirely a staff idea.

01:20:29.000 --> 01:20:30.999
Yes.

01:20:31.000 --> 01:20:32.999
The bare feet were a masterstroke.

01:20:33.000 --> 01:20:33.999
Seriously.

01:20:34.000 --> 01:20:34.999
I hadn't thought of it.

01:20:35.000 --> 01:20:36.999
If you'd worn shoes, I think

01:20:37.000 --> 01:20:37.999
the impact would have been weaker.

01:20:38.000 --> 01:20:38.999
It created that feeling.

01:20:39.000 --> 01:20:41.999
That feeling...

01:20:42.000 --> 01:20:43.999
Wildness.

01:20:44.000 --> 01:20:44.999
A primal quality.

01:20:45.000 --> 01:20:45.999
Right. And for the dance-break section,

01:20:46.000 --> 01:20:48.999
I also began from the feet.

01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:49.999
Right.

01:20:50.000 --> 01:20:50.999
So, in a way...

01:20:51.000 --> 01:20:53.999
I wanted to depict the spider

01:20:54.000 --> 01:20:55.999
entering my head

01:20:56.000 --> 01:20:58.999
and brainwashing me.

01:20:59.000 --> 01:21:01.999
It begins at the feet,

01:21:02.000 --> 01:21:03.999
climbs up through the hands,

01:21:04.000 --> 01:21:06.999
and enters the head.

01:21:07.000 --> 01:21:07.999
That's how I became the spider.

01:21:08.000 --> 01:21:08.999
It has that feeling.

01:21:09.000 --> 01:21:09.999
So you became the spider at the end.

01:21:10.000 --> 01:21:10.999
And then the spider...

01:21:11.000 --> 01:21:13.999
Yes, this was the key detail.

01:21:14.000 --> 01:21:15.999
I really remember this move.

01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:16.999
This, this—wow.

01:21:17.000 --> 01:21:17.999
Wow.

01:21:18.000 --> 01:21:18.999
That...

01:21:19.000 --> 01:21:20.999
Amazing. >> Where is that part

01:21:21.000 --> 01:21:22.999
where you're breathing heavily?

01:21:23.000 --> 01:21:24.999
I love the camera there.

01:21:25.000 --> 01:21:25.999
That shot...

01:21:26.000 --> 01:21:28.999
We practiced it so many times.

01:21:29.000 --> 01:21:31.999
It was unbelievable.

01:21:32.000 --> 01:21:32.999
Right. That camera shot was truly...

01:21:33.000 --> 01:21:34.999
If it moved even five centimeters forward,

01:21:35.000 --> 01:21:36.999
it would cover his face.

01:21:37.000 --> 01:21:38.999
Right. We aligned it many times.

01:21:39.000 --> 01:21:39.999
The camera enters at exactly that point.

01:21:40.000 --> 01:21:41.999
Yes, that's right.

01:21:42.000 --> 01:21:43.999
And at the start of the intro,

01:21:44.000 --> 01:21:45.999
you suddenly go like this. What was that?

01:21:46.000 --> 01:21:46.999
That strange move.

01:21:47.000 --> 01:21:47.999
From here...

01:21:48.000 --> 01:21:48.999
Yes.

01:21:49.000 --> 01:21:51.999
That strange move.

01:21:52.000 --> 01:21:52.999
Wow, that's not a spider.

01:21:53.000 --> 01:21:54.999
That wasn't solely my idea.

01:21:55.000 --> 01:21:57.999
I worked it out with an acquaintance

01:21:58.000 --> 01:22:00.999
who does acrobatics.

01:22:01.000 --> 01:22:02.999
We put down mats and kept rolling.

01:22:03.000 --> 01:22:03.999
That looked cool. We tried turning

01:22:04.000 --> 01:22:05.999
this way and that,

01:22:06.000 --> 01:22:07.999
and prepared diligently.

01:22:08.000 --> 01:22:10.999
We chose acrobatics I could perform live.

01:22:11.000 --> 01:22:13.999
And in the dance break, ja, you go—

01:22:14.000 --> 01:22:16.999
[Vocalizing]. Doesn't the friction

01:22:17.000 --> 01:22:17.999
between the floor and your bare feet burn?

01:22:18.000 --> 01:22:18.999
Your toenails can come off.

01:22:19.000 --> 01:22:20.999
Right, there's a lot of friction.

01:22:21.000 --> 01:22:21.999
You have to land on the callused part.

01:22:22.000 --> 01:22:23.999
On the flesh too...

01:22:24.000 --> 01:22:24.999
Ah, the direction of the flesh.

01:22:25.000 --> 01:22:26.999
That's right.

01:22:27.000 --> 01:22:28.999
You have to be careful. Yes.

01:22:29.000 --> 01:22:30.999
I think preparing the solo stage

01:22:31.000 --> 01:22:31.999
was a lot of fun.

01:22:32.000 --> 01:22:32.999
Yes, while doing it...

01:22:33.000 --> 01:22:33.999
That's good.

01:22:34.000 --> 01:22:35.999
The interesting thing is...

01:22:36.000 --> 01:22:38.999
And also...

01:22:39.000 --> 01:22:39.999
On top of that, yesterday...

01:22:40.000 --> 01:22:41.999
I changed the intro and outro

01:22:42.000 --> 01:22:42.999
quite a lot. >> How?

01:22:43.000 --> 01:22:44.999
Why didn't I notice? Why?

01:22:45.000 --> 01:22:45.999
I saw the intro expression.

01:22:46.000 --> 01:22:47.999
At first, you're lying like this.

01:22:48.000 --> 01:22:48.999
There were many differences.

01:22:49.000 --> 01:22:50.999
On day two, I lay like this.

01:22:51.000 --> 01:22:52.999
Ah.

01:22:53.000 --> 01:22:55.999
There were more subtle differences.

01:22:56.000 --> 01:22:57.999
Yes. And since this was

01:22:58.000 --> 01:22:59.999
our first concert in Korea...

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:01.999
There are overseas concertgoers

01:23:02.000 --> 01:23:03.999
and people who can't see every show,

01:23:04.000 --> 01:23:05.999
so I changed days one and two

01:23:06.000 --> 01:23:06.999
to offer more variety.

01:23:07.000 --> 01:23:09.999
I wanted them to have different feelings.

01:23:10.000 --> 01:23:12.999
Many people were curious

01:23:13.000 --> 01:23:13.999
about the ending poses

01:23:14.000 --> 01:23:15.999
and asked me about them.

01:23:16.000 --> 01:23:16.999
I did make them different.

01:23:17.000 --> 01:23:18.999
On day one I did this, and on day two

01:23:19.000 --> 01:23:20.999
I simply sat like this.

01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:23.999
There wasn't a deep meaning behind it.

01:23:24.000 --> 01:23:25.999
At that time, I hadn't planned

01:23:26.000 --> 01:23:27.999
an ending pose.

01:23:28.000 --> 01:23:28.999
It just came out.

01:23:29.000 --> 01:23:29.999
I decided to do whatever came naturally.

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:31.999
I thought, 'Just imagine I'm a spider.'

01:23:32.000 --> 01:23:33.999
And then...

01:23:34.000 --> 01:23:35.999
Maybe because I was tired,

01:23:36.000 --> 01:23:36.999
I ended up like this.

01:23:37.000 --> 01:23:38.999
You do look like a spider. Hey.

01:23:39.000 --> 01:23:41.999
So yes, it didn't have

01:23:42.000 --> 01:23:42.999
a profound meaning.

01:23:43.000 --> 01:23:44.999
There were no flaws, so even if

01:23:45.000 --> 01:23:45.999
I wanted to find fault,

01:23:46.000 --> 01:23:46.999
I couldn't.

01:23:47.000 --> 01:23:48.999
Want me to find one?

01:23:49.000 --> 01:23:49.999
Seriously, there were no flaws.

01:23:50.000 --> 01:23:51.999
It was perfect.

01:23:52.000 --> 01:23:52.999
Anyway, I prepared diligently,

01:23:53.000 --> 01:23:54.999
and you all loved it.

01:23:55.000 --> 01:23:55.999
Exactly.

01:23:56.000 --> 01:23:57.999
Seriously.

01:23:58.000 --> 01:23:58.999
I didn't know there was that whole story.

01:23:59.000 --> 01:24:00.999
Which story?

01:24:01.000 --> 01:24:03.999
That you filmed everything yourself

01:24:04.000 --> 01:24:05.999
and kept practicing to align it all.

01:24:06.000 --> 01:24:07.999
Ja, you filmed the draft yourself?

01:24:08.000 --> 01:24:09.999
Shall I show you after this? >> I want to see it.

01:24:10.000 --> 01:24:10.999
You even flew a drone—you went all in.

01:24:11.000 --> 01:24:11.999
But honestly...

01:24:12.000 --> 01:24:12.999
It couldn't be helped.

01:24:13.000 --> 01:24:14.999
We prepared our solo stages

01:24:15.000 --> 01:24:15.999
almost entirely on our own.

01:24:16.000 --> 01:24:18.999
Right? Until rehearsal, we each...

01:24:19.000 --> 01:24:20.999
We agreed to prepare them

01:24:21.000 --> 01:24:21.999
ourselves first.

01:24:22.000 --> 01:24:24.999
We each did a lot of preparation

01:24:25.000 --> 01:24:26.999
on our own.

01:24:27.000 --> 01:24:29.999
Right. >> So we didn't know

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:32.999
what the others were preparing

01:24:33.000 --> 01:24:35.999
or how they envisioned their stages.

01:24:36.000 --> 01:24:36.999
Even we...

01:24:37.000 --> 01:24:37.999
Didn't we first see them at rehearsal?

01:24:38.000 --> 01:24:38.999
Exactly.

01:24:39.000 --> 01:24:39.999
Yes.

01:24:40.000 --> 01:24:40.999
That's why, at the very first rehearsal,

01:24:41.000 --> 01:24:42.999
while the others rehearsed,

01:24:43.000 --> 01:24:45.999
we just kept going, 'Wow! This is insane!'

01:24:46.000 --> 01:24:48.999
And Yejun hyung helped me record 'Spider.'

01:24:49.000 --> 01:24:50.999
That's right.

01:24:51.000 --> 01:24:52.999
While helping,

01:24:53.000 --> 01:24:53.999
he refined some details.

01:24:54.000 --> 01:24:54.999
Of course.

01:24:55.000 --> 01:24:57.999
As expected. Great.

01:24:58.000 --> 01:24:59.999
In a word, it was a perfect stage.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:02.999
Hamin...

01:25:03.000 --> 01:25:03.999
Great.

01:25:04.000 --> 01:25:04.999
Ja, now...

01:25:05.000 --> 01:25:05.999
Ja, next...

01:25:06.000 --> 01:25:11.999
It's Noah's turn.

01:25:12.000 --> 01:25:14.999
I already talked quite a lot about this

01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:16.999
during a Weverse Live,

01:25:17.000 --> 01:25:17.999
actually.

01:25:18.000 --> 01:25:19.999
You shared some stories, but I didn't

01:25:20.000 --> 01:25:20.999
hear them, so please tell us again.

01:25:21.000 --> 01:25:22.999
Then, to summarize:

01:25:23.000 --> 01:25:25.999
before 'Good Boy Gone Bad,'

01:25:26.000 --> 01:25:27.999
I had quite a few other

01:25:28.000 --> 01:25:28.999
candidate songs.

01:25:29.000 --> 01:25:29.999
There were many.

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:31.999
A lot.

01:25:32.000 --> 01:25:33.999
Right. At first,

01:25:34.000 --> 01:25:36.999
I considered many songs that would

01:25:37.000 --> 01:25:38.999
showcase my vocal ability.

01:25:39.000 --> 01:25:39.999
Then...

01:25:40.000 --> 01:25:42.999
Second, I wanted a song whose vocals

01:25:43.000 --> 01:25:43.999
and lyrical message

01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:47.999
Oh.

01:25:48.000 --> 01:25:50.999
could offer more comfort and strength.

01:25:51.000 --> 01:25:52.999
But then the entertainment team suggested,

01:25:53.000 --> 01:25:54.999
'Since there's also a world tour,

01:25:55.000 --> 01:25:55.999
how about going

01:25:56.000 --> 01:25:57.999
a little more global?'

01:25:58.000 --> 01:26:00.999
That clicked immediately in my head.

01:26:01.000 --> 01:26:02.999
I thought, 'Yes, that's right.'

01:26:03.000 --> 01:26:03.999
Oh.

01:26:04.000 --> 01:26:06.999
I wondered what song would work.

01:26:07.000 --> 01:26:08.999
I'd always really liked

01:26:09.000 --> 01:26:10.999
'Good Boy Gone Bad,'

01:26:11.000 --> 01:26:12.999
and loved it from the first listen.

01:26:13.000 --> 01:26:14.999
So when I listened again,

01:26:15.000 --> 01:26:18.999
it seemed to contain

01:26:19.000 --> 01:26:20.999
every element I could perform

01:26:21.000 --> 01:26:21.999
and sing well.

01:26:22.000 --> 01:26:23.999
That's how it felt.

01:26:24.000 --> 01:26:27.999
It already uses breath so effectively.

01:26:28.000 --> 01:26:29.999
The feeling TXT sunbaenim gave it

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:31.999
turns rock-oriented in the chorus,

01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:33.999
and there's rap in the middle.

01:26:34.000 --> 01:26:35.999
Right. It condenses everything

01:26:36.000 --> 01:26:37.999
into one song.

01:26:38.000 --> 01:26:40.999
So I thought, 'This is the one.'

01:26:41.000 --> 01:26:42.999
But I wanted to make it

01:26:43.000 --> 01:26:45.999
more ominous.

01:26:46.000 --> 01:26:49.999
Since it was for the concert, I wanted it darker

01:26:50.000 --> 01:26:51.999
and more vampiric.

01:26:52.000 --> 01:26:53.999
We arranged it that way.

01:26:54.000 --> 01:26:56.999
You can hear a lot more piano on top.

01:26:57.000 --> 01:26:58.999
That makes the middle even more ominous.

01:26:59.000 --> 01:27:01.999
It feels like watching a horror film.

01:27:02.000 --> 01:27:02.999
I thought deeply about that.

01:27:03.000 --> 01:27:03.999
Mm.

01:27:04.000 --> 01:27:06.999
Once the song was chosen,

01:27:07.000 --> 01:27:09.999
it seemed like I should dance.

01:27:10.000 --> 01:27:12.999
But the original choreography,

01:27:13.000 --> 01:27:13.999
honestly...

01:27:14.000 --> 01:27:16.999
I thought it would be difficult

01:27:17.000 --> 01:27:18.999
to perform live by myself.

01:27:19.000 --> 01:27:20.999
After all, it was originally sung

01:27:21.000 --> 01:27:22.999
by five people.

01:27:23.000 --> 01:27:24.999
Yes. So...

01:27:25.000 --> 01:27:27.999
I asked the director

01:27:28.000 --> 01:27:31.999
to create choreography for me.

01:27:32.000 --> 01:27:34.999
A new version. >> Since it had become

01:27:35.000 --> 01:27:36.999
a newly arranged song.

01:27:37.000 --> 01:27:38.999
I explained that it had a vampire,

01:27:39.000 --> 01:27:40.999
Dracula-like concept.

01:27:41.000 --> 01:27:45.999
I wanted minimal demanding choreography

01:27:46.000 --> 01:27:47.999
and cool, gesture-focused movement.

01:27:48.000 --> 01:27:49.999
Wow, it was all planned.

01:27:50.000 --> 01:27:51.999
So the concept would be clearly visible.

01:27:52.000 --> 01:27:54.999
Yes. That was conveyed,

01:27:55.000 --> 01:27:55.999
and then they suddenly asked me,

01:27:56.000 --> 01:27:57.999
'Do you want choreography from verse to finish?'

01:27:58.000 --> 01:27:59.999
But I didn't want the verse

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:00.999
to feel choreographed.

01:28:01.000 --> 01:28:02.999
So only the chorus...

01:28:03.000 --> 01:28:05.999
I wanted choreography only in the chorus.

01:28:06.000 --> 01:28:07.999
So for the chorus...

01:28:08.000 --> 01:28:09.999
Apart from those parts,

01:28:10.000 --> 01:28:11.999
I prepared my own gestures.

01:28:12.000 --> 01:28:12.999
That's how I did it.

