02:00:18.000 --> 02:00:19.999
We removed some elements

02:00:20.000 --> 02:00:22.999
and emphasized the parts

02:00:23.000 --> 02:00:25.999
that could become cool rock.

02:00:26.000 --> 02:00:27.999
One major reason it suited

02:00:28.000 --> 02:00:29.999
a rock arrangement

02:00:30.000 --> 02:00:32.999
was Eunho's section in 'Virtual Idol.'

02:00:33.000 --> 02:00:34.999
That's the key.

02:00:35.000 --> 02:00:37.999
Without it, suddenly turning

02:00:38.000 --> 02:00:39.999
'Virtual Idol' into rock wouldn't have worked.

02:00:40.000 --> 02:00:43.999
Right. The original recording

02:00:44.000 --> 02:00:46.999
contains that mock news report.

02:00:47.000 --> 02:00:48.999
You know the original song.

02:00:49.000 --> 02:00:50.999
We wanted to use that part in the concert,

02:00:51.000 --> 02:00:54.999
but I understand there were

02:00:55.000 --> 02:00:55.999
copyright issues.

02:00:56.000 --> 02:00:57.999
So we couldn't use it.

02:00:58.000 --> 02:01:00.999
Behind the scenes, I almost

02:01:01.000 --> 02:01:03.999
recorded a replacement.

02:01:04.000 --> 02:01:05.999
Someone suggested it to me.

02:01:06.000 --> 02:01:07.999
Right.

02:01:08.000 --> 02:01:09.999
Show us once.

02:01:10.000 --> 02:01:12.999
A mock report about a virtual idol

02:01:13.000 --> 02:01:14.999
causing a sensation and rising in popularity.

02:01:15.000 --> 02:01:15.999
Something like that.

02:01:16.000 --> 02:01:17.999
Why are you so good at it?

02:01:18.000 --> 02:01:19.999
They should have simply asked you.

02:01:20.000 --> 02:01:22.999
I didn't know it had been removed either.

02:01:23.000 --> 02:01:23.999
It played through rehearsal.

02:01:24.000 --> 02:01:27.999
Anyway, I had to rap there.

02:01:28.000 --> 02:01:29.999
But rapping doesn't make me nervous.

02:01:30.000 --> 02:01:31.999
Rapping is...

02:01:32.000 --> 02:01:33.999
This is my bragging rap,

02:01:34.000 --> 02:01:37.999
so I can't sound nervous.

02:01:38.000 --> 02:01:39.999
It's about our...

02:01:40.000 --> 02:01:46.999
These lyrics...

02:01:47.000 --> 02:01:48.999
What? >> Wait, when did you prepare that?

02:01:49.000 --> 02:01:50.999
After ten o'clock...

02:01:51.000 --> 02:01:51.999
Once it passed ten,

02:01:52.000 --> 02:01:52.999
I was no longer entirely sane.

02:01:53.000 --> 02:01:54.999
We worked so hard today.

02:01:55.000 --> 02:01:56.999
How should we take this?

02:01:57.000 --> 02:01:58.999
Your momentum was so strong.

02:01:59.000 --> 02:01:59.999
He keeps going until it becomes funny.

02:02:00.000 --> 02:02:01.999
But aren't your feet cold?

02:02:02.000 --> 02:02:03.999
Your feet are freezing.

02:02:04.000 --> 02:02:04.999
It's time now.

02:02:05.000 --> 02:02:07.999
At least put on socks.

02:02:08.000 --> 02:02:08.999
Would you like some socks?

02:02:09.000 --> 02:02:12.999
Exactly. Put gloves on them if necessary.

02:02:13.000 --> 02:02:14.999
Ja, anyway.

02:02:15.000 --> 02:02:16.999
As you can tell from the lyrics,

02:02:17.000 --> 02:02:18.999
they require confidence.

02:02:19.000 --> 02:02:19.999
I didn't write them timidly,

02:02:20.000 --> 02:02:21.999
because they were meant to make

02:02:22.000 --> 02:02:24.999
our PLLI feel proud.

02:02:25.000 --> 02:02:25.999
Those are the kind of lyrics they are.

02:02:26.000 --> 02:02:29.999
Anyway, I thought we should

02:02:30.000 --> 02:02:31.999
turn up the atmosphere

02:02:32.000 --> 02:02:32.999
and get everyone jumping.

02:02:33.000 --> 02:02:34.999
Oh, right. I felt sorry about something.

02:02:35.000 --> 02:02:35.999
I just remembered.

02:02:36.000 --> 02:02:37.999
I think it happened on day one.

02:02:38.000 --> 02:02:40.999
While Eunho rapped, I tried to double him,

02:02:41.000 --> 02:02:42.999
but I think I came in wrong.

02:02:43.000 --> 02:02:43.999
Didn't you miss it once?

02:02:44.000 --> 02:02:46.999
I did. I couldn't hear the beat.

02:02:47.000 --> 02:02:48.999
I doubled the wrong beat.

02:02:49.000 --> 02:02:50.999
I entered at the wrong moment.

02:02:51.000 --> 02:02:53.999
How? >> I lost track of where I was.

02:02:54.000 --> 02:02:56.999
The place I meant to come in...

02:02:57.000 --> 02:02:59.999
I think it was around the 'prophet' part.

02:03:00.000 --> 02:03:01.999
'Prophet.'

02:03:02.000 --> 02:03:03.999
Yes. I waited for the beat

02:03:04.000 --> 02:03:05.999
and said it, but there was still a long pause.

02:03:06.000 --> 02:03:07.999
I'd entered much too early.

02:03:08.000 --> 02:03:09.999
And he stumbled immediately after.

02:03:10.000 --> 02:03:12.999
I did stumble.

02:03:13.000 --> 02:03:14.999
For a moment, I thought,

02:03:15.000 --> 02:03:17.999
'Did I make him stumble? I'm sorry.'

02:03:18.000 --> 02:03:21.999
So I decided not to double anymore.

02:03:22.000 --> 02:03:22.999
I didn't notice.

02:03:23.000 --> 02:03:24.999
I became timid and stayed quiet.

02:03:25.000 --> 02:03:27.999
Yes, that happened.

02:03:28.000 --> 02:03:29.999
Anyway, I felt very proud.

02:03:30.000 --> 02:03:33.999
PLLI often tell us

02:03:34.000 --> 02:03:35.999
that those lyrics make them feel proud.

02:03:36.000 --> 02:03:36.999
Right, right.

02:03:37.000 --> 02:03:38.999
The rap contains much of our story,

02:03:39.000 --> 02:03:41.999
and at Munhak, while descending

02:03:42.000 --> 02:03:43.999
on the lift...

02:03:44.000 --> 02:03:47.999
singing it made me realize

02:03:48.000 --> 02:03:49.999
how far we'd truly come.

02:03:50.000 --> 02:03:52.999
PLAVE had traveled so many roads

02:03:53.000 --> 02:03:53.999
together with PLLI.

02:03:54.000 --> 02:03:55.999
It made my heart burn with emotion.

02:03:56.000 --> 02:03:57.999
Right. I get chills

02:03:58.000 --> 02:03:58.999
every time I hear it.

02:03:59.000 --> 02:04:00.999
It was so good. Well done.

02:04:01.000 --> 02:04:01.999
Yes. >> Seriously, well done.

02:04:02.000 --> 02:04:02.999
You're so good.

02:04:03.000 --> 02:04:05.999
You rode the lift well too.

02:04:06.000 --> 02:04:06.999
When you jumped, weren't you scared?

02:04:07.000 --> 02:04:09.999
I was. I don't have a fear of heights,

02:04:10.000 --> 02:04:11.999
but it was quite high.

02:04:12.000 --> 02:04:13.999
Hamin jumps from even higher places,

02:04:14.000 --> 02:04:14.999
so he's fine.

02:04:15.000 --> 02:04:15.999
I do that often.

02:04:16.000 --> 02:04:17.999
Because you're a cat.

02:04:18.000 --> 02:04:20.999
But people call me a puppy,

02:04:21.000 --> 02:04:21.999
so...

02:04:22.000 --> 02:04:22.999
Yes.

02:04:23.000 --> 02:04:24.999
I'm scared of high places.

02:04:25.000 --> 02:04:26.999
As it descended...

02:04:27.000 --> 02:04:28.999
It was scary. >> Everyone came down like this.

02:04:29.000 --> 02:04:30.999
So I jumped from a low height

02:04:31.000 --> 02:04:31.999
at the end—boing.

02:04:32.000 --> 02:04:32.999
From nice and low.

02:04:33.000 --> 02:04:34.999
Yes. Then I entered in the rock-arranged

02:04:35.000 --> 02:04:37.999
version of 'Virtual Idol.'

02:04:38.000 --> 02:04:38.999
You led that part very well.

02:04:39.000 --> 02:04:39.999
Right? Right?

02:04:40.000 --> 02:04:45.999
Exactly.

02:04:46.000 --> 02:04:48.999
It was a very enjoyable stage.

02:04:49.000 --> 02:04:51.999
We should move on now,

02:04:52.000 --> 02:04:53.999
because there's so much to discuss.

02:04:54.000 --> 02:04:54.999
We need to talk about 'Born Savage,'

02:04:55.000 --> 02:04:57.999
where a huge number of dancers

02:04:58.000 --> 02:04:59.999
appeared.

02:05:00.000 --> 02:05:00.999
They were zombie dancers.

02:05:01.000 --> 02:05:01.999
Zom...

02:05:02.000 --> 02:05:04.999
I think that may have been our first time

02:05:05.000 --> 02:05:06.999
showing dancers

02:05:07.000 --> 02:05:09.999
onstage with us. How was it?

02:05:10.000 --> 02:05:10.999
Mm.

02:05:11.000 --> 02:05:12.999
It definitely made the stage

02:05:13.000 --> 02:05:16.999
feel more alive and impactful.

02:05:17.000 --> 02:05:18.999
It surprised many PLLI too.

02:05:19.000 --> 02:05:19.999
Right.

02:05:20.000 --> 02:05:21.999
It was a full mega-crew

02:05:22.000 --> 02:05:22.999
performance.

02:05:23.000 --> 02:05:25.999
Right. Yes.

02:05:26.000 --> 02:05:27.999
I think it was a good experiment,

02:05:28.000 --> 02:05:29.999
and you can expect even more ahead.

02:05:30.000 --> 02:05:31.999
We have so much left

02:05:32.000 --> 02:05:34.999
to show you.

02:05:35.000 --> 02:05:36.999
We prepared it almost as a declaration.

02:05:37.000 --> 02:05:38.999
It's something we'd dreamed about

02:05:39.000 --> 02:05:42.999
since our very beginning:

02:05:43.000 --> 02:05:43.999
performing together

02:05:44.000 --> 02:05:45.999
with dancers on the same stage.

02:05:46.000 --> 02:05:46.999
That was always the dream.

02:05:47.000 --> 02:05:48.999
We finally did it this time,

02:05:49.000 --> 02:05:50.999
and it went so successfully.

02:05:51.000 --> 02:05:51.999
It was wonderful.

02:05:52.000 --> 02:05:53.999
And PLLI also really

02:05:54.000 --> 02:05:56.999
loved our 'Born Savage'

02:05:57.000 --> 02:05:57.999
outfits.

02:05:58.000 --> 02:06:00.999
Why did they love them? My odyssey

02:06:01.000 --> 02:06:03.999
was right here. They loved the odyssey.

02:06:04.000 --> 02:06:06.999
Odysseus.

02:06:07.000 --> 02:06:07.999
Oh.

02:06:08.000 --> 02:06:09.999
They loved them so much.

02:06:10.000 --> 02:06:11.999
There was a little more exposure.

02:06:12.000 --> 02:06:12.999
They liked that.

02:06:13.000 --> 02:06:14.999
Right?

02:06:15.000 --> 02:06:15.999
Yes. You could see our body lines,

02:06:16.000 --> 02:06:18.999
so they liked it.

02:06:19.000 --> 02:06:19.999
Is that why? Then one day,

02:06:20.000 --> 02:06:22.999
we'll reveal our abs completely.

02:06:23.000 --> 02:06:24.999
If you do that...

02:06:25.000 --> 02:06:25.999
Yes.

02:06:26.000 --> 02:06:28.999
Dduks, you're watching, right?

02:06:29.000 --> 02:06:30.999
Someday. Anyway, people really loved it.

02:06:31.000 --> 02:06:32.999
I think they did.

02:06:33.000 --> 02:06:33.999
'Born Savage' was wonderful.

02:06:34.000 --> 02:06:35.999
Ja, now let's talk about

02:06:36.000 --> 02:06:37.999
'Pump Up The Volume!'

02:06:38.000 --> 02:06:40.999
Previously, we wore

02:06:41.000 --> 02:06:42.999
college-student varsity jackets.

02:06:43.000 --> 02:06:44.999
This time we gave you a completely

02:06:45.000 --> 02:06:47.999
different office-worker look.

02:06:48.000 --> 02:06:50.999
I thought it looked very cool.

02:06:51.000 --> 02:06:52.999
This kind of feeling worked well too.

02:06:53.000 --> 02:06:54.999
What did you think?

02:06:55.000 --> 02:06:58.999
I genuinely felt as though we'd grown.

02:06:59.000 --> 02:07:00.999
I wondered whether I'd matured,

02:07:01.000 --> 02:07:02.999
and that moved me.

02:07:03.000 --> 02:07:04.999
I think 'Pump Up The Volume!' has a story.

02:07:05.000 --> 02:07:06.999
At first, we were at school.

02:07:07.000 --> 02:07:09.999
Right.

02:07:10.000 --> 02:07:12.999
It was like a growth process.

02:07:13.000 --> 02:07:14.999
We were in school,

02:07:15.000 --> 02:07:18.999
and now the song made me feel we'd grown up.

02:07:19.000 --> 02:07:19.999
Then what will come next?

02:07:20.000 --> 02:07:21.999
This time...

02:07:22.000 --> 02:07:23.999
We've reached the company now.

02:07:24.000 --> 02:07:25.999
If we've reached the company, where next?

02:07:26.000 --> 02:07:27.999
What comes after that?

02:07:28.000 --> 02:07:29.999
Next could be becoming the boss

02:07:30.000 --> 02:07:32.999
or company representative.

02:07:33.000 --> 02:07:36.999
The representative. The CEO.

02:07:37.000 --> 02:07:37.999
CEO. >> Good.

02:07:38.000 --> 02:07:38.999
Now, CEO...

02:07:39.000 --> 02:07:40.999
What does a CEO wear?

02:07:41.000 --> 02:07:44.999
What kind of look is this?

02:07:45.000 --> 02:07:47.999
That could be dangerous. A young CEO.

02:07:48.000 --> 02:07:48.999
Great.

02:07:49.000 --> 02:07:50.999
Anyway, we're also excited

02:07:51.000 --> 02:07:52.999
to see what comes next.

02:07:53.000 --> 02:07:55.999
It should be fun.

02:07:56.000 --> 02:07:57.999
It was also a one-take sequence.

02:07:58.000 --> 02:07:59.999
I found that very fun.

02:08:00.000 --> 02:08:02.999
The way it began backstage

02:08:03.000 --> 02:08:06.999
was an interesting composition.

02:08:07.000 --> 02:08:08.999
Outside of concert preparation,

02:08:09.000 --> 02:08:10.999
we sometimes hold meetings

02:08:11.000 --> 02:08:12.999
with our company representative

02:08:13.000 --> 02:08:15.999
about future stages.

02:08:16.000 --> 02:08:17.999
Before the previous concert,

02:08:18.000 --> 02:08:18.999
we said,

02:08:19.000 --> 02:08:20.999
'We'd like to try

02:08:21.000 --> 02:08:23.999
what other singers do,

02:08:24.000 --> 02:08:26.999
starting a performance backstage someday.'

02:08:27.000 --> 02:08:28.999
They made that happen here.

02:08:29.000 --> 02:08:30.999
Yes. It fit 'Pump Up The Volume!'

02:08:31.000 --> 02:08:33.999
perfectly.

02:08:34.000 --> 02:08:36.999
They wove it in so naturally.

02:08:37.000 --> 02:08:38.999
It suited the song so well.

02:08:39.000 --> 02:08:41.999
The comments suggest that after the CEO,

02:08:42.000 --> 02:08:43.999
we should go to a wedding.

02:08:44.000 --> 02:08:45.999
A wedding.

02:08:46.000 --> 02:08:46.999
As grooms...

02:08:47.000 --> 02:08:48.999
What about the dress?

02:08:49.000 --> 02:08:49.999
Imagine PLLI entering from the front,

02:08:50.000 --> 02:08:52.999
as if from the bride's point of view.

02:08:53.000 --> 02:08:53.999
And so on.

02:08:54.000 --> 02:08:55.999
These ideas are appearing in the comments.

02:08:56.000 --> 02:08:57.999
That's excellent.

02:08:58.000 --> 02:08:58.999
There's also the reception.

02:08:59.000 --> 02:09:00.999
Right.

02:09:01.000 --> 02:09:02.999
I think we might really do this.

02:09:03.000 --> 02:09:03.999
Then the doors open...

02:09:04.000 --> 02:09:07.999
This might become a spoiler.

02:09:08.000 --> 02:09:09.999
But I truly hope our concerts

02:09:10.000 --> 02:09:11.999
continue as one connected story.

02:09:12.000 --> 02:09:14.999
Someday,

02:09:15.000 --> 02:09:16.999
when all our hair is white,

02:09:17.000 --> 02:09:17.999
we'll still be onstage.

02:09:18.000 --> 02:09:18.999
Yes. >> That would be cool too.

02:09:19.000 --> 02:09:20.999
It would. So cool.

02:09:21.000 --> 02:09:22.999
Wouldn't it be beautiful?

02:09:23.000 --> 02:09:25.999
Taking another spoonful of Munhak's story

02:09:26.000 --> 02:09:27.999
and weaving it into the next concert

02:09:28.000 --> 02:09:29.999
would be wonderful. >> I like that.

02:09:30.000 --> 02:09:30.999
Great.

02:09:31.000 --> 02:09:32.999
Ja, and we also revealed

02:09:33.000 --> 02:09:34.999
that performance

02:09:35.000 --> 02:09:36.999
for the first time.

02:09:37.000 --> 02:09:39.999
We practiced so much.

02:09:40.000 --> 02:09:41.999
We have many stories to tell about it.

02:09:42.000 --> 02:09:45.999
There are rehearsal stories too.

02:09:46.000 --> 02:09:47.999
May I share one?

02:09:48.000 --> 02:09:49.999
After the concert,

02:09:50.000 --> 02:09:52.999
I contacted Aiki-nim separately.

02:09:53.000 --> 02:09:55.999
Really? >> I thanked her for coming

02:09:56.000 --> 02:09:57.999
and said that PLLI loved

02:09:58.000 --> 02:10:00.999
the choreography.

02:10:01.000 --> 02:10:04.999
Jiyeon and ODD also came

02:10:05.000 --> 02:10:06.999
for that section,

02:10:07.000 --> 02:10:09.999
but I was so overwhelmed by the stage

02:10:10.000 --> 02:10:11.999
that I couldn't speak with them.

02:10:12.000 --> 02:10:13.999
Right.

02:10:14.000 --> 02:10:16.999
They came to watch too,

02:10:17.000 --> 02:10:17.999
and I worried they'd feel disappointed.

02:10:18.000 --> 02:10:19.999
It stayed on my mind, so I contacted them.

02:10:20.000 --> 02:10:22.999
Well done. >> They said it was fine,

02:10:23.000 --> 02:10:23.999
that the stage looked amazing,

02:10:24.000 --> 02:10:26.999
and that PLLI were incredible.

02:10:27.000 --> 02:10:29.999
Thank you so much for creating

02:10:30.000 --> 02:10:30.999
such wonderful choreography.

02:10:31.000 --> 02:10:31.999
Thank you very much.

02:10:32.000 --> 02:10:34.999
You saw the choreography draft video

02:10:35.000 --> 02:10:35.999
that was uploaded, right?

02:10:36.000 --> 02:10:37.999
It showed their understanding

02:10:38.000 --> 02:10:39.999
of us and of PLLI.

02:10:40.000 --> 02:10:44.999
Right.

02:10:45.000 --> 02:10:46.999
They had studied us so deeply

02:10:47.000 --> 02:10:48.999
and showed us so much affection.

02:10:49.000 --> 02:10:50.999
That moved me.

02:10:51.000 --> 02:10:53.999
Even during the first lesson, they brought

02:10:54.000 --> 02:10:55.999
so much energy.

02:10:56.000 --> 02:10:58.999
They held many separate meetings

02:10:59.000 --> 02:11:01.999
with Hamin and me,

02:11:02.000 --> 02:11:03.999
asking what we thought

02:11:04.000 --> 02:11:04.999
and what else we wanted to add.

02:11:05.000 --> 02:11:05.999
They asked us so many questions

02:11:06.000 --> 02:11:07.999
like that.

02:11:08.000 --> 02:11:09.999
It was wonderful.

02:11:10.000 --> 02:11:13.999
Yes, it was such an enjoyable

02:11:14.000 --> 02:11:15.999
learning experience.

02:11:16.000 --> 02:11:17.999
They taught us with so much energy.

02:11:18.000 --> 02:11:20.999
Eunho...

02:11:21.000 --> 02:11:23.999
I loved the chemistry between Jiyeon

02:11:24.000 --> 02:11:24.999
and Eunho.

02:11:25.000 --> 02:11:25.999
Eunho unnie?

02:11:26.000 --> 02:11:27.999
I never taught you choreography like that.

02:11:28.000 --> 02:11:28.999
Sorry.

02:11:29.000 --> 02:11:30.999
Eunho unnie.

02:11:31.000 --> 02:11:32.999
But anyway...

02:11:33.000 --> 02:11:34.999
That energy helped so much,

02:11:35.000 --> 02:11:36.999
and made practice much more

02:11:37.000 --> 02:11:37.999
fun.

02:11:38.000 --> 02:11:39.999
It made me work harder.

02:11:40.000 --> 02:11:41.999
It also gave me this determination:

02:11:42.000 --> 02:11:44.999
'I really won't make a mistake this time.'

02:11:45.000 --> 02:11:46.999
They watched us that closely,

02:11:47.000 --> 02:11:49.999
so I felt

02:11:50.000 --> 02:11:52.999
that they truly cared

02:11:53.000 --> 02:11:53.999
for us.

02:11:54.000 --> 02:11:56.999
It raised our fighting spirit.

02:11:57.000 --> 02:11:57.999
Their passion was incredible.

02:11:58.000 --> 02:11:58.999
Practice was as fun as the song itself.

02:11:59.000 --> 02:12:00.999
Right.

02:12:01.000 --> 02:12:03.999
When we'd be talking, they'd call, 'One, two!'

